From 8285205262faccd5975aead9a184ad9a55458865 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeFiChain community contributor (AI-assisted, Claude) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:56:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] consensus: reject overflowing transfer sums
 (SumAllTransfers), DF25

SumAllTransfers() ignored the Res returned by CBalances::AddBalances().
When a per-token addition overflowed CAmount, CBalances::Add() returned an
error without touching the sum, so the overflowing amount (and any further
tokens of that recipient) silently dropped out of the total while every
recipient was still credited in full.

Exploited on mainnet with AccountToAccount (one small amount + an amount
that overflows the sum, to two different recipients):
- block 6564035, tx c0248c39...cfef0e (03.11.2026 00:13 UTC)
- block 6566081, tx bc2e5a68...b2e8ac (03.11.2026 19:02 UTC)
Each debited only the small amount and credited ~92.23 bn DFI.

Affected consensus paths: AccountToAccount, AnyAccountsToAccounts,
UtxosToAccount (sum compared with burnt amount) and AddPoolLiquidity
(sum smaller than debited amounts).

From DF25Height these paths use SumAllTransfersChecked(), which
rejects non-positive amounts and per-token overflow. Below DF25Height the
legacy behaviour is kept so historical blocks still validate.

Mainnet DF25Height is set to 6566082 (earliest height that keeps all
known blocks valid) and must be confirmed by the Development SIG;
6564035 would make both exploit blocks invalid.

Adds balances_tests.cpp documenting the legacy behaviour and the fix.

